WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.882
Hi! Is it a apple or an apple? How do we say one cat and two cats? Today we'll learn about nouns.

2
00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:14.034
A noun names a person, animal, thing or place.

3
00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:18.234
Use a before a consonant sound: a cat, a ball.

4
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:22.146
Use an before a vowel sound: an apple, an egg.

5
00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:26.898
An ant, an umbrella: easier to say.

6
00:00:27.048 --> 00:00:30.522
For more than one, add s: two cats.

7
00:00:30.672 --> 00:00:33.282
A book becomes three books.

8
00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:37.290
Don't use a before a plural: cats, not a cats.

9
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.946
Use plurals after some and many too.

10
00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:45.330
Watch out! We don't say a egg!

11
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.714
Egg starts with the vowel e, so use an.

12
00:00:48.864 --> 00:00:52.938
An egg is easier to say too.

13
00:00:53.088 --> 00:01:02.058
Your turn! I see, ___, owl. A or an? Pause and think.

14
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:07.938
Owl starts with the vowel o, so an. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:08.088 --> 00:01:17.490
Another one! She has, ___, dog. A or an? Pause and think.

16
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.058
Dog starts with d, so a. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:32.058
Here's another! Two, ___. Pen or pens? Pause and think.

18
00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:37.842
More than one needs s: pens. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:46.890
Try one more! ___, orange. A or an? Pause and think.

20
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.338
Orange starts with o, so an. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:52.488 --> 00:02:01.578
Try one more! I have three, ___. Which is right? Pause and think.

22
00:02:01.728 --> 00:02:07.410
Three means more than one: balls. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:15.450
Try one more! Which word is a noun? Pause and think.

24
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.282
Cake names a thing, so it's a noun. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:30.186
Try one more! ___, bus. A or an? Pause and think.

26
00:02:30.336 --> 00:02:35.610
Bus starts with b, so a. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:43.602
Last one! One box, two, ___. Pause and think.

28
00:02:43.752 --> 00:02:49.601
Box adds es: boxes. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:49.751 --> 00:02:56.585
Remember: a before consonants, an before vowels. Add s for more than one, and drop the a.

30
00:02:56.736 --> 00:03:01.793
Count things at home and say two cups, three chairs!

